\id COL - Open English Translation—Readers’ Version (OET-RV) v0.2.2
\usfm 3.0
\ide UTF-8
\h Colossians
\toc1 Paul’s letter to the believers in Colossae
\toc2 Colossians
\mt2 Paul’s letter to the believers in
\mt1 Colossae
\rem This is still an early look into the unpolished text of the Open English Translation of the Bible. Please double-check the text in advance before using in public.
\c 1
\p
\v 1 \add This letter is from\add* Paul, a missionary of Messiah Jesus by God’s will, and \add from\add* our brother Timothy.
\p
\v 2 To the people \add there\add* in Colossae who are godly and faithful brothers and sisters in Messiah.
\p Grace and peace to you all from God our father and \add the\add* master Jesus Messiah.
\s1 Paul’s thanks and prayers
\p
\v 3 We thank God, \add the\add* father of our master Jesus Messiah as we continually pray for you all,
\v 4 after having heard about your faith in Messiah Jesus and the love that you have for all godly people
\v 5 which arose because of your hope in a heavenly reward. You all previously heard about that in the message of the truth—the good message
\v 6 that’s in you and that’s bearing fruit in the world and growing, just like it did among all of you from the day that you heard \add it\add* and knew about the grace of God in truth.
\v 7 You all learnt that from Epaphras, our dearly loved fellow slave who’s our faithful servant of the messiah,
\v 8 and he’s the one who made your love in \add the\add* spirit evident to us.
\p
\v 9 It’s because of that that we haven’t stopped praying from the time that we heard it, and requesting that you all would be filled with the knowledge of his will in all wisdom and spiritual insight,
\v 10 to live worthily of the master—pleasing him in every \add kind of\add* good and productive work. We pray that you all will grow in the knowledge of God
\v 11 and be strengthened with all power, according to his great power, \add leading to\add* endurance and patience with contentment.
\v 12 Then you’ll all be thanking the father, the one who qualified you all for a part of the inheritance of godly people \add who live\add* in the light.
\v 13 The father rescued us from the power of darkness and redirected us into the kingdom of his dear son—
\v 14 the one who buys us out of slavery and forgives our sins.
\s1 Jesus is both the first and the highest
\p
\v 15 The son is the \add visible\add* image of the invisible God, the firstborn of all creation
\v 16 because it was him who created everything in the heavens and on the earth, both visible and invisible, including all authorities such as kingdoms and governments. \add Yes,\add* everything was created by him and for him.
\v 17 He came before everything and everything \add still\add* only exists because of him.
\v 18 He is the head of the body which is the assembly. He is the beginning, the first of the dead to come back to life, so that he would be the first in everything,
\v 19 because God was pleased to live in him in all totality
\v 20 and to reconcile everything to himself through him—both things on earth and things in the heavens. God made peace through him by means of the blood at the \add execution\add* post.
\p
\v 21 Once all of you were alienated \add from God\add*—your thinking was that of an enemy and your actions were evil,
\v 22 but now you all have been reconciled by means of the death of Jesus’ physical body. He’s able to present you as pure and blameless in front of God—unable to be charged for any infraction
\v 23 if indeed you continue on in your established and firm faith. Don’t let \add anyone\add* drive away the hope that \add comes from\add* the good message that you all heard and which has been declared throughout the whole world—it’s that good message that I’ve become a servant of.
\s1 Paul’s work for believers
\p
\v 24 So now I’m happy to be suffering for you all, and I’m catching up in my body to the tribulations of the messiah in his body, which is the assembly.
\v 25 I became a servant of the assembly under God’s supervision when he gave me the \add work\add* of fulfilling God’s message—
\v 26 the mystery which had been hidden away from the generations over the ages, but which was recently revealed to his chosen people.
\v 27 God wanted them to explain the riches of this incredible mystery among the pagans: \add the\add* messiah in you all bringing the hope of reaching God.
\v 28 \add Yes,\add* Messiah who we are telling everyone about as we teach and recommend to everyone, so that we might present every person \add made\add* perfect in Messiah.
\v 29 That’s what I’m working hard towards according to his work as well—working in me with power.
\c 2
\p
\v 1 I want you all to know how much I struggle for you and for those in Laodicea and for those who’ve never actually set eyes on me.
\v 2 \add By knowing that,\add* their hearts may be comforted, having been held together in love and to all the riches of the full assurance of the insight, to the knowledge of the mystery of God, Messiah. WHAT DOES THIS MEAN?
\v 3 \add He holds\add* all the treasures of wisdom and secret knowledge.
\p
\v 4 I’m telling you all this so that none of you will be deceived by persuasive talk,
\v 5 because even though I’m physically far way, I’m with you all in the spirit. I’m pleased to see the sensibleness and firmness of your faith in Messiah.
\s1 Living in Messiah
\p
\v 6 So in the same way that you all received the messiah, Jesus the master, keep living in him.
\v 7 You’ve already been rooted in him and then built up and confirmed in the faith just as all of you were taught, and been very thankful.
\p
\v 8 Be careful in case anyone captures \add your minds\add* with fancy ideas or theories without proof that come from human traditions or from worldly thinking, and not from Messiah.
\v 9 Every component of the greatness of God lives in his \add human\add* body,
\v 10 and you also have been completed and are in him. He is the head of all rule and authority.
\p
\v 11 It wasn’t just human hands that circumcised you by \add cutting off part of the body\add*, but Messiah circumcised you all by cutting you away from your sinful acts.
\v 12 You all were buried with him when you were immersed \add in water\add*, and you came back to life with him when you came up \add from the water\add*, through faith in God’s working which gave him life after death.
\v 13 You all were dead in your disobedience and because your bodies were ‘uncircumcised’. Then he made us alive together with him after he forgave us for all our disobedience.
\v 14 He erased the writing that listed the charges against us and so it was removed—nailed to the \add execution\add* post.
\v 15 He had disarmed the rulers and authorities and publicly exposed them, because he had won the victory over them on the post.\f + \fr 2:15 \ft The meaning of the Greek ‘ἐν αὐτῷ’ literally ‘in it/him’ isn’t clear here and leads to two common translations: a/ ‘on/in him’, or as we have chosen (interpreting the ‘it’ to be referring back to ‘σταυρῷ’ ‘execution post’ from the previous verse), ‘on the post’.\f*
\p
\v 16 Don’t let anyone judge you all about what you eat or drink, or about \add observing\add* feasts or holidays or days of rest.
\v 17 They’re just shadows of what’s coming, but the body \add causing the shadow\add* is that of the messiah.
\v 18 Don’t let anyone be disqualifying you all with their \add apparent\add* humility and worshipping the messengers, telling you what they’ve seen and being arrogant and vain about their earthly minds.
\v 19 They’re not listening to the head which controls all the joints and ligaments of the body and holds it all together as God causes it to grow.
\s1 From death to life with the messiah
\p
\v 20 If you’ve died to worldly principles, then why are you letting yourselves be indoctrinated with worldly living:
\v 21 ‘Don’t hold this. Don’t taste that. Don’t touch this.’
\v 22 \add No,\add* All those \add rules\add* lead to corruption when they’re used as the commands and teaching of humans.
\v 23 They seem to be wise and make you more religious or humble as you strictly obey them, \add but\add* don’t honour \add the realities\add* of our worldly desires.
\c 3
\p
\v 1 So if you all were brought back to life along with the messiah, then be concerned with discovering the things from above where the messiah is sitting on God’s right.
\v 2 \add Yes,\add* be thinking about things from above, not earthly things
\v 3 because you’ve all ‘died’ and your lives have been hidden in God with the messiah.
\v 4 When he’s revealed \add on his return\add*, then your lives will also be revealed with him in GLORY.
\s1 The old and new lives
\p
\v 5 So put your earthly natures to death: sexual immorality, impurity, passion, evil desires, and greediness which is idolatry,
\v 6 because those things invoke God’s severe anger.
\v 7 You all used to do those things when you lived in them.
\p
\v 8 But now, don’t let any of these things come out of your mouth: severe anger, rage, malice, slander, or profanity.
\v 9 Don’t lie to each other, because you’ve gotten rid of the ‘old person’ and their habits.
\v 10 So ‘dress’ in the ‘new person’ who’s renewed with the knowledge of being in the image of the creator,
\v 11 where there’s no distinctions between ethnicities or religion, locals and foreigners, slaves or free, but Messiah is everything and in all \add of us\add*.
\p
\v 12 So as holy people chosen and loved by God, ‘dress’ in: compassionate hearts, kindness, humility, gentleness, patience,
\v 13 tolerating each other, and forgiving anyone who has a complaint about another person. The master forgave all of you, so you also should forgive \add others\add*.
\v 14 Then over all of those, ‘dress’ in love which is the perfect connection \add to others\add*.
\v 15 Let the peace of the messiah rule in your hearts. That’s what you were called to \add as parts of\add* one body. Make sure that you’re thankful
\v 16 and that the messiah’s message is a rich part of you with all its wisdom as you teach and give advice to each other. Sing psalms and hymns and spiritual songs to God with thankfulness in your hearts.
\v 17 Then give thanks to God the father through the name of Messiah Jesus in everything—whatever you’re all saying or doing.
\s1 Advice by role
\p
\v 18 You wives should be subject to your husbands to the degree that it’s fitting in Yahweh.
\p
\v 19 You husbands should love your wives—don’t become bitter towards them.
\p
\v 20 You children should obey your parents in everything, because that pleases Yahweh.
\p
\v 21 You fathers shouldn’t be exasperating your children otherwise they may become discouraged.
\p
\v 22 You slaves should submit to your human masters in everything, not just when they’re watching like others do, but sincerely, and so honouring the master.
\p
\v 23 Whatever you all might be doing, consider in your hearts that you’re working for the master and not for people,
\v 24 knowing that Yahweh will repay you with an inheritance because you’ve been serving the master messiah.
\v 25 Anyone who’s doing wrong will be repaid for that wrongness, and there won’t be any favouritism.
\c 4
\p
\v 1 You masters, ensure that you’re treating your slaves with goodness and equality, knowing that you all also have \add a\add* master \add of your own\add* in heaven.
\s1 Further teaching for believers
\p
\v 2 Persevere in prayer, keeping watch and being thankful.
\v 3 Pray together for us as well that God would open a door for us \add to share\add* the message—to tell \add about\add* the mystery of the messiah. That’s also why I’m in chains—
\v 4 so that I can explain the mystery whenever I have an opportunity to speak.
\p
\v 5 Use wisdom as you all walk towards non-believers, using the time wisely.
\v 6 Always show grace in your conversations, like a meal that’s seasoned with salt, so you’ll know how to answer each person in their situation.
\s1 Final greetings
\p
\v 7 My dear brother and faithful servant and fellow slave, Tychicus, will tell you all about me.
\v 8 I’m sending him to all of you \add there\add* so you’ll find out the \add news\add* that concerns you all and so that he can comfort you \add there\add*.
\v 9 The faithful and dear brother, Onesimus, who’s from your place will also be with him.
\p
\v 10 My fellow prisoner, Aristarchus, sends his greetings along with Barnabas’ cousin, Mark. You’ve already received instructions about that, so accept him if he arrives \add there\add*.
\v 11 Jesus who’s nicknamed Justus also sends his greetings. These guys are from strict Jewish backgrounds, but they’re my only fellow-workers for God’s kingdom who became an encouragement to me.
\p
\v 12 Epaphras sends his greetings. He’s \add another\add* one from your place and a slave of messiah Jesus who always prays for you that you will stand mature and fully confident in all of God’s will.
\v 13 I can assure you that he has strong concerns for you all, as well as those in Laodicea and in Hierapolis.
\v 14 The dear doctor Luke greets you all, as does Demas.
\p
\v 15 Give my greetings to the brothers and sisters in Laodicea, and to Nympha and the assembly \add that meets\add* in her house,
\v 16 and whenever my letter gets read to you all, make sure that it’s also read to those from the assembly in Laodicea, and that you all \add also\add* read their letter.
\v 17 Tell Archippus to make sure to fulfil the duties that Yahweh gave him to do.
\p
\v 18 \sig I, Paul, am writing this \+add final\+add* greeting in my own handwriting. Remember me \+add here\+add* in chains.\sig*
\p \sig May God’s grace be with all of you.\sig*
